{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we need to determine the probability that a three-digit number with a units digit of 6 is divisible by 6. A number is divisible by 6 if and only if it is divisible by both 2 and 3. Since the units digit is 6, the number is already divisible by 2. Therefore, we only need to check for divisibility by 3.\n\nA number is divisible by 3 if the sum of its digits is divisible by 3. Let's denote the three-digit number as \\( \\overline{abc} \\), where \\( c = 6 \\). The number can be written as \\( 100a + 10b + 6 \\). The sum of the digits is \\( a + b + 6 \\). We need \\( a + b + 6 \\) to be divisible by 3.\n\nFirst, we determine the range of possible values for \\( a \\) and \\( b \\). Since \\( a \\) is the hundreds digit of a three-digit number, \\( a \\) can be any digit from 1 to 9. The digit \\( b \\) can be any digit from 0 to 9. Therefore, there are \\( 9 \\times 10 = 90 \\) possible three-digit numbers with a units digit of 6.\n\nNext, we need to count how many of these numbers have a sum of digits \\( a + b + 6 \\) that is divisible by 3. For each fixed value of \\( a \\), \\( b \\) can be any digit from 0 to 9, and we need \\( a + b + 6 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{3} \\). This is equivalent to \\( b \\equiv -a - 6 \\pmod{3} \\), or \\( b \\equiv 3 - a \\pmod{3} \\) (since \\(-6 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{3}\\)).\n\n","prefix_end":1287,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1184,311,8253,279,18927,429,264,2326,48342,1372,448,264,8153,15723,315,220,21,374,74916,553,220,21,13,362,1372,374,74916,553,220,21,421,323,1172,421,432,374,74916,553,2176,220,17,323,220,18,13,8704,279,8153,15723,374,220,21,11,279,1372,374,2669,74916,553,220,17,13,15277,11,582,1172,1184,311,1779,369,49368,3147,553,220,18,382,32,1372,374,74916,553,220,18,421,279,2629,315,1181,18509,374,74916,553,220,18,13,6771,594,7806